    "56106": {
        "order_id": 10,
        "exam_type": "WAEC",
        "subject": "Auto Mechanics",
        "topic": "Brake system principles",
        "question_type": "Objective",
        "exam_year": "2023",
        "question_text": "<p>In a hydraulic brake system, what principle explains why a small force applied at the brake pedal results in a larger force at the wheel cylinders?</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>The hydraulic brake system operates on <b>Pascal's Law</b>, which states that pressure applied to a confined fluid is transmitted undiminished throughout the fluid. This allows a small force at the brake pedal to be multiplied at the wheel cylinders.</p>",
        "reference_passage": null,
        "novel": null,
        "comments_count": 0,
        "options": [
